IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `snap-core`

-- LAYER 1 (the law, objectively): section 2031 of the Food and Nutrition Act of 2008 (7 U.S.C. 2031), "Minnesota Family
-- Investment Project", lines 2842-2949 of usc07-ch51.txt (snap6's second range).
-- SOURCE: a plain-text rendering made by a converter script from the OLRC's USLM XML. It is not the official text, and
-- nothing here is "verified against the official text".
-- READING A RESULT: a MAYBE BOOLEAN, MAYBE NUMBER or MAYBE DATE answers JUST FALSE only where the text says no in its own words,
-- JUST TRUE where it says yes, and NOTHING everywhere else ("not covered"). Every branch says which kind it is.
-- MONEY is a NUMBER of dollars. DATES are `Date day month year`.
-- "The Project" is the family investment demonstration project of the State of Minnesota. "The State" is Minnesota (j)(4); the
-- core has `the State agency` and no party for the State government, so duties of "the State" are put on `the State agency`
-- (fork FR-31-5). A participating family is `the household`. The Comptroller General has no party in the core (NEEDS-CORE.md).
-- SEAMS: what other sections answer is taken as an input named for the answering section (SEAMS.md).

-- HELPERS (not a rule of the Act): three-valued AND / OR over MAYBE BOOLEAN, so that a NOTHING input is passed through
-- unless another limb decides the answer without it (PLAN.md section 4).
GIVEN xs IS A LIST OF MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2031 every one of these holds` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF elem (JUST FALSE) xs THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): one limb is the text's no, so the whole is, wherever that no came from
        IF elem NOTHING xs THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): a limb is not covered and no other limb says no
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE   -- TRUE-kind: every limb holds

GIVEN xs IS A LIST OF MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2031 at least one of these holds` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF elem (JUST TRUE) xs THEN JUST TRUE   -- TRUE-kind: one limb holds
        IF elem NOTHING xs THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): a limb is not covered and no other limb holds
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): every limb is the text's no

§ `s 2031 -- Minnesota Family Investment Project`

-- TYPES this section needs (none is in the core).

-- (j)(3): how a person is related to the minor child, for the definition of "caregiver".
DECLARE `s 2031 relationship to the minor child` IS ONE OF
    `s 2031 natural or adoptive parent`
    `s 2031 grandfather`
    `s 2031 grandmother`
    `s 2031 brother`
    `s 2031 sister`
    `s 2031 stepfather`
    `s 2031 stepmother`
    `s 2031 stepbrother`
    `s 2031 stepsister`
    `s 2031 uncle`
    `s 2031 aunt`
    `s 2031 first cousin`
    `s 2031 nephew`
    `s 2031 niece`
    `s 2031 a person of a preceding generation denoted by the prefix great or great-great`
    `s 2031 a spouse of any person named above, even after the marriage ends by death or divorce`
    `s 2031 some other relationship`

-- (j)(1): the facts about a group of people who live together.
DECLARE `s 2031 group` HAS
    `they live together`                                                        IS A BOOLEAN
    `the number of minor children`                                              IS A NUMBER
    `the minor children are related to each other as siblings, half siblings, stepsiblings, or adopted siblings` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a natural or adoptive parent of the children lives with them`              IS A BOOLEAN
    `the children's caregiver lives with them`                                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is a pregnant woman in the third trimester of pregnancy with no children` IS A BOOLEAN

-- (b)(5): how a family is selected for the Project.
DECLARE `s 2031 way of selecting a family` IS ONE OF
    `s 2031 by submission and approval of an application for participation in the Project`
    `s 2031 by assigning a family determined eligible for or participating in the part A of title IV program or the supplemental nutrition assistance program`
    `s 2031 in some other way`

-- (b)(10)(B)(i): why a family's participation in the Project ended.
DECLARE `s 2031 why participation ended` IS ONE OF
    `s 2031 the Project is terminated`
    `s 2031 the family or member is determined ineligible for the Project because of income`
    `s 2031 the family or member is determined ineligible for the Project because of resources`
    `s 2031 the family or member is determined ineligible for the Project because of a change in household composition`
    `s 2031 some other reason`

-- (b)(14)(B): who ends the Project.
DECLARE `s 2031 who terminates the Project` IS ONE OF
    `s 2031 the State, on notice to the Secretary`
    `s 2031 the Secretary, after notice and an opportunity for a hearing, on finding that the State materially failed to comply`
    `s 2031 the State and the Secretary jointly agree`

-- (c)(1): the facts about a parent in a participating family.
DECLARE `s 2031 parent` HAS
    `the family has one parent`                                            IS A BOOLEAN
    `the parent is ill or incapacitated`                                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `the parent's age in years`                                            IS A NUMBER
    `the parent is needed in the home because of the illness or incapacity of another family member` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the age of the parent's youngest child in months, or a negative number if the parent has no child` IS A NUMBER
    `the parent personally provides care for the child`                    IS A BOOLEAN
    `the hours a week the parent is employed or participates in education or employment and training services` IS A NUMBER
    `the number of hours the parent works a week can be verified`          IS A BOOLEAN
    `the hours a week the parent works, if they can be verified`           IS A NUMBER
    `the parent's earnings a week`                                         IS A NUMBER
    `the trimester of pregnancy, or 0 if the parent is not pregnant`       IS A NUMBER

-- (i)(1): what the evaluation plan the State develops contains.
DECLARE `s 2031 evaluation plan` HAS
    `it provides for an independent evaluation designed to provide reliable information on Project impacts and implementation` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it includes treatment and control groups with random assignment of families in an urban setting` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it satisfies the evaluation concerns of the Secretary of Agriculture` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it takes into consideration the evaluation requirements and administrative obligations of the State` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it measures the effects of the Project on the goals of increasing family income, prevention of long-term dependency, movement toward self-support, and simplification of the welfare system` IS A BOOLEAN

-- the acts the State agency and the Secretary are told to do, for the regulative rules.
DECLARE `s 2031 act` IS ONE OF
    `s 2031 determine eligibility for the Project and issue assistance to eligible families`
    `s 2031 give the individual an application form and permit its filing`
    `s 2031 restrict the number of families who may be represented by such person`
    `s 2031 establish criteria and verification standards for representation`
    `s 2031 notify the family of the supplemental nutrition assistance program and whom to contact`
    `s 2031 continue to pay from State funds an amount equal to the food assistance portion`
    `s 2031 pay the State the value of the benefits`
    `s 2031 give the family or family member a specific request for the additional information, with assistance in completing a signed application`
    `s 2031 determine whether the family is eligible for the supplemental nutrition assistance program`
    `s 2031 carry out the supplemental nutrition assistance program throughout the State`
    `s 2031 approve the application`
    `s 2031 pay the State each calendar quarter`
    `s 2031 adjust the payments made to the State`
    `s 2031 waive compliance with a requirement of this chapter`
    `s 2031 develop and implement a plan for an independent evaluation`

§§ `(a) In general`

-- (a)(2) "The Project may be implemented only in accordance with this section and only if the Secretary of Health and Human
-- Services approves an application submitted by the State permitting the State to include in the Project families who are
-- eligible to receive benefits under part A of title IV of the Social Security Act." An "only" bars; satisfying it grants nothing.
-- src:2845 | (2) The Project may be implemented only in accordance with this section and only if the Secretary of Health and Human Services approves an application submitted by the State permitting the State to include in the Project families who are eligible to receive benefits under part A of title IV of the Social Security Act.
@ref s 2031(a)(2) (src:2845)
GIVEN `the Project is implemented in accordance with this section` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Secretary of Health and Human Services approved an application permitting the State to include families eligible under part A of title IV` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2031(a)(2) the Project may be implemented` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the Project is implemented in accordance with this section` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The Project may be implemented only in accordance with this section"
        IF `the Secretary of Health and Human Services approved an application permitting the State to include families eligible under part A of title IV` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "and only if the Secretary of Health and Human Services approves an application"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "only" bars and grants nothing; the grant is in (a)(1)

-- (a)(1) "Subject to paragraph (2), upon written application of the State of Minnesota that complies with this section ..., and
-- after approval of such application by the Secretary in accordance with subsections (b) and (d), the State may implement a family
-- investment demonstration project".
-- src:2844 | (1) Subject to paragraph (2), upon written application of the State of Minnesota that complies with this section and sections 6 to 11, 13, 130, and 132 of article 5 of 282 of the 1989 Laws of Minnesota, and after approval of such application by the Secretary in accordance with subsections (b) and (d), the State may implement a family investment demonstration project (hereinafter in this section referred to as the “Project”) in parts of the State to determine whether the Project more effectively helps families to become self-supporting and enhances their ability to care for their children than do the supplemental nutrition assistance program and programs under parts A and F [Footnote: 1 See References in Text note below.] of title IV of the Social Security Act [42 U.S.C. 601 et seq.]. The State may provide cash payments under the Project, subject to paragraph (2), that replace assistance otherwise available under the supplemental nutrition assistance program and under part A of title IV of the Social Security Act.
@ref s 2031(a)(1) (src:2844)
GIVEN `the written application of the State of Minnesota complies with this section and sections 6 to 11, 13, 130, and 132 of article 5 of 282 of the 1989 Laws of Minnesota` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Secretary approved the application in accordance with subsections (b) and (d)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the Project may be implemented under paragraph (2)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2031(a)(1) the State may implement the Project` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the Project may be implemented under paragraph (2)` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subject to paragraph (2)" carries paragraph (2)'s "only" ("The Project may be implemented only in accordance with this section and only if ...")
        IF `the written application of the State of Minnesota complies with this section and sections 6 to 11, 13, 130, and 132 of article 5 of 282 of the 1989 Laws of Minnesota` AND `the Secretary approved the application in accordance with subsections (b) and (d)` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE   -- TRUE-kind: "upon written application of the State of Minnesota that complies ..., and after approval of such application by the Secretary ..., the State may implement a family investment demonstration project"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "upon written application ... and after approval" are not words that make a missing step the text's no

§§ `(b) Required terms and conditions of Project`

-- (b) "The application submitted by the State under subsection (a) shall provide an assurance that the Project shall satisfy all of
-- the following requirements". Whether the application complies with subsection (b) (as (d)(1) asks) is taken to be whether it
-- provides that assurance (fork FR-31-2).
-- src:2847 | The application submitted by the State under subsection (a) shall provide an assurance that the Project shall satisfy all of the following requirements:
@ref s 2031(b) the assurance (src:2847)
GIVEN `the application submitted by the State under subsection (a) provides an assurance that the Project shall satisfy all of the requirements of this subsection` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2031(b) the application complies with the requirements specified in subsection (b)` MEANS
    IF `the application submitted by the State under subsection (a) provides an assurance that the Project shall satisfy all of the requirements of this subsection`
    THEN JUST TRUE   -- TRUE-kind: "shall provide an assurance that the Project shall satisfy all of the following requirements"
    ELSE NOTHING     -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text says what the application shall provide and not what follows if it does not

-- (b)(1) "Only families may be eligible to receive assistance and services through the Project."
-- src:2848 | (1) Only families may be eligible to receive assistance and services through the Project.
@ref s 2031(b)(1) (src:2848)
GIVEN `s 2031(j)(1) the group is a family` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2031(b)(1) the group may be eligible to receive assistance and services through the Project` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 2031(j)(1) the group is a family`
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Only families may be eligible to receive assistance and services through the Project"
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "only" bars others and grants nothing to a family
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the group is a family was not supplied

-- (b)(2) "Participating families, families eligible for or participating in the program authorized under part A of title IV ...
-- or the supplemental nutrition assistance program that are assigned to and found eligible for the Project, and families required
-- to submit an application for the Project that are found eligible for the Project shall be ineligible to receive benefits under
-- the supplemental nutrition assistance program."
-- src:2849 | (2) Participating families, families eligible for or participating in the program authorized under part A of title IV of the Social Security Act [42 U.S.C. 601 et seq.] or the supplemental nutrition assistance program that are assigned to and found eligible for the Project, and families required to submit an application for the Project that are found eligible for the Project shall be ineligible to receive benefits under the supplemental nutrition assistance program.
@ref s 2031(b)(2) (src:2849)
GIVEN `the family participates in the Project` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the family is eligible for or participating in the part A of title IV program or the supplemental nutrition assistance program, and is assigned to and found eligible for the Project` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the family is required to submit an application for the Project and is found eligible for the Project` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2031(b)(2) the family may receive benefits under the supplemental nutrition assistance program` MEANS
    IF `the family participates in the Project`
       OR `the family is eligible for or participating in the part A of title IV program or the supplemental nutrition assistance program, and is assigned to and found eligible for the Project`
       OR `the family is required to submit an application for the Project and is found eligible for the Project`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall be ineligible to receive benefits under the supplemental nutrition assistance program"
    ELSE NOTHING      -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): (b)(2) names three kinds of family

-- (b)(3)(A) "Subject to the provisions of this paragraph and any reduction imposed under subsection (c)(3), the value of
-- assistance provided to participating families shall not be less than the aggregate value of the assistance such families could
-- receive under the supplemental nutrition assistance program and part A of title IV if such families did not participate in the Project."
-- src:2850 | (3)
-- src:2851 | (A) Subject to the provisions of this paragraph and any reduction imposed under subsection (c)(3) of this section, the value of assistance provided to participating families shall not be less than the aggregate value of the assistance such families could receive under the supplemental nutrition assistance program and part A of title IV of the Social Security Act if such families did not participate in the Project.
@ref s 2031(b)(3)(A) (src:2850-2851)
GIVEN `the value of the assistance provided under the Project, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the aggregate value of the assistance the family could receive under the supplemental nutrition assistance program and part A of title IV if it did not participate, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the reduction imposed under subsection (c)(3), in dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2031(b)(3)(A) the value of the assistance is enough` MEANS
    IF `the value of the assistance provided under the Project, in dollars` AT LEAST `the aggregate value of the assistance the family could receive under the supplemental nutrition assistance program and part A of title IV if it did not participate, in dollars` MINUS `the reduction imposed under subsection (c)(3), in dollars`
    THEN JUST TRUE   -- TRUE-kind: "shall not be less than the aggregate value" is met
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the value of assistance provided to participating families shall not be less than the aggregate value of the assistance such families could receive"

-- (b)(3)(B)(i) and (ii) "payments for child care expenses under the Project shall be considered part of the value of assistance
-- provided to participating families with earnings; payments for child care expenses for families without earnings shall not be
-- considered part of the value of assistance provided ... or the aggregate value of assistance".
-- src:2852 | (B) For purposes of satisfying the requirement specified in subparagraph (A)—
-- src:2853 | (i) payments for child care expenses under the Project shall be considered part of the value of assistance provided to participating families with earnings;
-- src:2854 | (ii) payments for child care expenses for families without earnings shall not be considered part of the value of assistance provided to participating families or the aggregate value of assistance that such families could have received under the supplemental nutrition assistance program and part A of title IV of the Social Security Act; and
@ref s 2031(b)(3)(B)(i) and (ii) (src:2852-2854)
GIVEN `the assistance under the Project other than child care payments, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the payments for child care expenses under the Project, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the family has earnings` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 2031(b)(3)(B) the value of assistance provided, counting child care as the text counts it, in dollars` MEANS
    IF `the family has earnings`
    THEN `the assistance under the Project other than child care payments, in dollars` PLUS `the payments for child care expenses under the Project, in dollars`   -- (i) "shall be considered part of the value of assistance provided to participating families with earnings"
    ELSE `the assistance under the Project other than child care payments, in dollars`   -- (ii) "for families without earnings shall not be considered part of the value of assistance provided"

-- (b)(3)(B)(iii) "any child support payments not assigned to the State under the provisions of part A of title IV ..., less $50
-- per month, shall be considered part of the aggregate value of assistance participating families would receive if such families
-- did not participate in the Project". The amount counted is the payments less $50, and not below nothing.
-- src:2855 | (iii) any child support payments not assigned to the State under the provisions of part A of title IV of the Social Security Act, less $50 per month, shall be considered part of the aggregate value of assistance participating families would receive if such families did not participate in the Project;
@ref s 2031(b)(3)(B)(iii) (src:2855)
GIVEN `the child support payments not assigned to the State in a month, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 2031(b)(3)(B)(iii) the child support counted in the aggregate value for a month, in dollars` MEANS
    IF `the child support payments not assigned to the State in a month, in dollars` GREATER THAN 50
    THEN `the child support payments not assigned to the State in a month, in dollars` MINUS 50
    ELSE 0

-- (b)(3)(C) "the State shall (i) identify the sets of characteristics indicative of families that might receive less assistance
-- under the Project; (ii) establish a mechanism to determine, for each participating family that has a set of characteristics
-- identified under clause (i) whether such family could receive more assistance, in the aggregate ... if such family did not
-- participate in the project; (iii) increase the amount of assistance provided under the Project to any family that could receive
-- more ... so that the assistance provided under the Project to such family is not less than the aggregate amount ...; and (iv)
-- increase the amount of assistance paid to participating families, if the State or locality imposes a sales tax on food, by the
-- amount needed to compensate for the tax. This subparagraph shall not be construed to require the State to make the determination
-- under clause (ii) for families that do not have a set of characteristics identified under clause (i)."
-- src:2857 | (i) identify the sets of characteristics indicative of families that might receive less assistance under the Project;
@ref s 2031(b)(3)(C)(i) identify the sets of characteristics (src:2857)
GIVEN `the State has identified the sets of characteristics indicative of families that might receive less assistance under the Project` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2031(b)(3)(C)(i) the State has identified the sets of characteristics` MEANS
    IF `the State has identified the sets of characteristics indicative of families that might receive less assistance under the Project`
    THEN JUST TRUE   -- TRUE-kind: "the State shall (i) identify the sets of characteristics indicative of families that might receive less assistance under the Project"
    ELSE NOTHING     -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text says what the State shall do and not what follows if it does not

-- src:2856 | (C) For purposes of satisfying the requirement specified in subparagraph (A), the State shall—
-- src:2857 | (i) identify the sets of characteristics indicative of families that might receive less assistance under the Project;
-- src:2858 | (ii) establish a mechanism to determine, for each participating family that has a set of characteristics identified under clause (i) whether such family could receive more assistance, in the aggregate, under the supplemental nutrition assistance program and part A of title IV of the Social Security Act if such family did not participate in the project;
-- src:2859 | (iii) increase the amount of assistance provided under the Project to any family that could receive more assistance, in the aggregate, under the supplemental nutrition assistance program and part A of title IV of the Social Security Act if such family did not participate in the Project, so that the assistance provided under the Project to such family is not less than the aggregate amount of assistance such family could receive under the supplemental nutrition assistance program and part A of title IV of the Social Security Act if such family did not participate in the Project; and
-- src:2860 | (iv) increase the amount of assistance paid to participating families, if the State or locality imposes a sales tax on food, by the amount needed to compensate for the tax.
-- src:2861 | This subparagraph shall not be construed to require the State to make the determination under clause (ii) for families that do not have a set of characteristics identified under clause (i).
@ref s 2031(b)(3)(C)(ii) and the last sentence (src:2856-2861)
GIVEN `the family has a set of characteristics identified under clause (i)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2031(b)(3)(C) the State shall make the determination for the family` MEANS
    IF `the family has a set of characteristics identified under clause (i)`
    THEN JUST TRUE   -- TRUE-kind: "establish a mechanism to determine, for each participating family that has a set of characteristics identified under clause (i)"
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This subparagraph shall not be construed to require the State to make the determination under clause (ii) for families that do not have a set of characteristics identified under clause (i)"

-- src:2859 | (iii) increase the amount of assistance provided under the Project to any family that could receive more assistance, in the aggregate, under the supplemental nutrition assistance program and part A of title IV of the Social Security Act if such family did not participate in the Project, so that the assistance provided under the Project to such family is not less than the aggregate amount of assistance such family could receive under the supplemental nutrition assistance program and part A of title IV of the Social Security Act if such family did not participate in the Project; and
@ref s 2031(b)(3)(C)(iii) (src:2859)
GIVEN `the aggregate amount the family could receive under the supplemental nutrition assistance program and part A of title IV if it did not participate, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the assistance provided under the Project to the family, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 2031(b)(3)(C)(iii) the increase the State shall make in the assistance, in dollars` MEANS
    IF `the aggregate amount the family could receive under the supplemental nutrition assistance program and part A of title IV if it did not participate, in dollars` GREATER THAN `the assistance provided under the Project to the family, in dollars`
    THEN `the aggregate amount the family could receive under the supplemental nutrition assistance program and part A of title IV if it did not participate, in dollars` MINUS `the assistance provided under the Project to the family, in dollars`   -- "so that the assistance provided under the Project to such family is not less than the aggregate amount"
    ELSE 0   -- no increase is needed to reach that aggregate amount

-- src:2860 | (iv) increase the amount of assistance paid to participating families, if the State or locality imposes a sales tax on food, by the amount needed to compensate for the tax.
-- src:2861 | This subparagraph shall not be construed to require the State to make the determination under clause (ii) for families that do not have a set of characteristics identified under clause (i).
@ref s 2031(b)(3)(C)(iv) the increase is owed if the State or locality imposes a sales tax (src:2860-2861)
GIVEN `the State or locality imposes a sales tax on food` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2031(b)(3)(C)(iv) the State shall increase the amount of assistance paid to participating families for the sales tax` MEANS
    IF `the State or locality imposes a sales tax on food`
    THEN JUST TRUE   -- TRUE-kind: "increase the amount of assistance paid to participating families, if the State or locality imposes a sales tax on food"
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): a failed "if the State or locality imposes a sales tax on food" (marginal reading (a))

-- src:2860 | (iv) increase the amount of assistance paid to participating families, if the State or locality imposes a sales tax on food, by the amount needed to compensate for the tax.
@ref s 2031(b)(3)(C)(iv) (src:2860)
GIVEN `the State or locality imposes a sales tax on food` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount needed to compensate for the tax, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 2031(b)(3)(C)(iv) the increase for the sales tax, in dollars` MEANS
    IF `the State or locality imposes a sales tax on food`
    THEN JUST `the amount needed to compensate for the tax, in dollars`   -- "increase the amount of assistance paid to participating families, if the State or locality imposes a sales tax on food, by the amount needed to compensate for the tax"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the increase is owed "if the State or locality imposes a sales tax on food"

-- (b)(3)(D)(i) "The State shall designate standardized amounts of assistance provided as food assistance under the Project and
-- notify monthly each participating family of such designated amount."
-- src:2863 | (i) The State shall designate standardized amounts of assistance provided as food assistance under the Project and notify monthly each participating family of such designated amount.
@ref s 2031(b)(3)(D)(i) designate standardized amounts and notify monthly (src:2863)
GIVEN `the State has designated standardized amounts of assistance provided as food assistance under the Project` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the State has notified the participating family of the designated amount this month` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2031(b)(3)(D)(i) the State has designated the amounts and notified the family` MEANS
    IF `the State has designated standardized amounts of assistance provided as food assistance under the Project` AND `the State has notified the participating family of the designated amount this month`
    THEN JUST TRUE   -- TRUE-kind: "The State shall designate standardized amounts of assistance provided as food assistance under the Project and notify monthly each participating family of such designated amount"
    ELSE NOTHING     -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text says what the State shall do and not what follows if it does not

-- (b)(3)(D)(i)-(iii) "The State shall designate standardized amounts of assistance provided as food assistance under the Project
-- and notify monthly each participating family of such designated amount. The amount of food assistance so designated shall be at
-- least the value of benefits such family could have received under the supplemental nutrition assistance program if the Project
-- had not been implemented. ... The State shall periodically allow participating families the option to receive such food
-- assistance in the form of benefits."
-- src:2864 | (ii) The amount of food assistance so designated shall be at least the value of benefits such family could have received under the supplemental nutrition assistance program if the Project had not been implemented. The provisions of this subparagraph shall not require that the State make individual determinations as to the amount of assistance under the Project designated as food assistance.
@ref s 2031(b)(3)(D)(ii) (src:2864)
GIVEN `the food assistance designated for the family, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the value of benefits the family could have received under the supplemental nutrition assistance program if the Project had not been implemented, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2031(b)(3)(D)(ii) the designated food assistance is enough` MEANS
    IF `the food assistance designated for the family, in dollars` AT LEAST `the value of benefits the family could have received under the supplemental nutrition assistance program if the Project had not been implemented, in dollars`
    THEN JUST TRUE   -- TRUE-kind: "shall be at least the value of benefits such family could have received" is met
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The amount of food assistance so designated shall be at least the value of benefits"

-- (b)(3)(D)(iii) "The State shall periodically allow participating families the option to receive such food assistance in the form of benefits."
-- "Periodically" is not defined, so only the fact that the option was allowed is tested.
-- src:2865 | (iii) The State shall periodically allow participating families the option to receive such food assistance in the form of benefits.
@ref s 2031(b)(3)(D)(iii) the option to receive the food assistance as benefits (src:2865)
GIVEN `the State has allowed the participating family the option to receive such food assistance in the form of benefits` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2031(b)(3)(D)(iii) the State has allowed the family the option` MEANS
    IF `the State has allowed the participating family the option to receive such food assistance in the form of benefits`
    THEN JUST TRUE   -- TRUE-kind: "The State shall periodically allow participating families the option to receive such food assistance in the form of benefits"
    ELSE NOTHING     -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): "periodically" is not defined, and the text says nothing of what follows if the option is not allowed

-- (b)(3)(E) "(i) Individuals ineligible for the Project who are members of a household including a participating family shall
-- have their eligibility for the supplemental nutrition assistance program determined and have their benefits calculated and
-- issued following the standards established under the supplemental nutrition assistance program, except as provided differently in
-- this subparagraph. (ii) ... without regard to the participating family. (iii) In computing such individuals' income ..., the State
-- agency shall apply the maximum excess shelter expense deduction specified under section 2014(e) of this title. (iv) Such
-- individuals' monthly allotment shall be the higher of $10 or 75 percent of the amount calculated following the standards of the
-- supplemental nutrition assistance program and the foregoing requirements of this subparagraph, rounded to the nearest lower whole
-- dollar." The calculated amount (with the maximum excess shelter expense deduction applied) is the answer of sections 2014 and 2017.
-- src:2867 | (i) Individuals ineligible for the Project who are members of a household including a participating family shall have their eligibility for the supplemental nutrition assistance program determined and have their benefits calculated and issued following the standards established under the supplemental nutrition assistance program, except as provided differently in this subparagraph.
@ref s 2031(b)(3)(E)(i) eligibility and benefits follow the standards of the supplemental nutrition assistance program (src:2867)
GIVEN `the individual is ineligible for the Project and is a member of a household including a participating family` IS A BOOLEAN
      `eligibility has been determined and benefits calculated and issued following the standards established under the supplemental nutrition assistance program, except as provided differently in subparagraph (E)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2031(b)(3)(E)(i) the individual's eligibility and benefits follow the standards of the supplemental nutrition assistance program` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the individual is ineligible for the Project and is a member of a household including a participating family` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Individuals ineligible for the Project who are members of a household including a participating family"
        IF `eligibility has been determined and benefits calculated and issued following the standards established under the supplemental nutrition assistance program, except as provided differently in subparagraph (E)` THEN JUST TRUE   -- TRUE-kind: "shall have their eligibility for the supplemental nutrition assistance program determined and have their benefits calculated and issued following the standards"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text says what shall be done and not what follows if it is not

-- src:2868 | (ii) The State agency shall determine such individuals’ eligibility for benefits under the supplemental nutrition assistance program and the amount of such benefits without regard to the participating family.
