        IF `the State provides a method for reviewing its application and distributing assistance to it` THEN JUST TRUE   -- TRUE-kind: "the State shall provide a method for reviewing applications ... and distributing assistance"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text says what the State shall provide and not what follows if it does not

-- (b)(7) "Whenever selection for participation in the Project is accomplished by assigning families that are determined eligible
-- for or participating in the program authorized by part A of title IV ... or the supplemental nutrition assistance program".
-- src:2883 | (7) Whenever selection for participation in the Project is accomplished by assigning families that are determined eligible for or participating in the program authorized by part A of title IV of the Social Security Act or the supplemental nutrition assistance program—
@ref s 2031(b)(7) lead-in (src:2883)
GIVEN way IS A `s 2031 way of selecting a family`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 2031(b)(7) selection is accomplished by assigning families that are determined eligible for or participating in the part A of title IV program or the supplemental nutrition assistance program` MEANS
    CONSIDER way
    WHEN `s 2031 by assigning a family determined eligible for or participating in the part A of title IV program or the supplemental nutrition assistance program` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- (b)(7)(A) "the State shall provide eligible families assistance under the Project no later than benefits would have been
-- provided following the standards established under the supplemental nutrition assistance program". The date those benefits
-- would have been provided is the answer of the administration section (the text does not cite it), so it is an input.
-- src:2884 | (A) the State shall provide eligible families assistance under the Project no later than benefits would have been provided following the standards established under the supplemental nutrition assistance program; and
@ref s 2031(b)(7)(A) assistance no later than benefits would have been provided (src:2884)
GIVEN way IS A `s 2031 way of selecting a family`
      `the date the State provides the eligible family assistance under the Project` IS A DATE
      `s 2020 the date benefits would have been provided following the standards established under the supplemental nutrition assistance program` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2031(b)(7)(A) the assistance is provided no later than the benefits would have been` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 2020 the date benefits would have been provided following the standards established under the supplemental nutrition assistance program`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the date the standards of the supplemental nutrition assistance program give was not supplied
    WHEN JUST latest THEN
        BRANCH
            IF NOT (`s 2031(b)(7) selection is accomplished by assigning families that are determined eligible for or participating in the part A of title IV program or the supplemental nutrition assistance program` way) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the lead-in of paragraph (7)
            IF `the date the State provides the eligible family assistance under the Project` AT MOST latest THEN JUST TRUE   -- TRUE-kind: "no later than benefits would have been provided"
            OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall provide eligible families assistance under the Project no later than benefits would have been provided"

-- (b)(7)(B) "the State shall ensure that assistance under the Project is provided so that there is no interruption in benefits for
-- families participating in the program under part A of title IV ... or the supplemental nutrition assistance program."
-- src:2885 | (B) the State shall ensure that assistance under the Project is provided so that there is no interruption in benefits for families participating in the program under part A of title IV of the Social Security Act or the supplemental nutrition assistance program.
@ref s 2031(b)(7)(B) no interruption in benefits (src:2885)
GIVEN way IS A `s 2031 way of selecting a family`
      `there is an interruption in benefits for a family participating in the part A of title IV program or the supplemental nutrition assistance program` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2031(b)(7)(B) the State has ensured that there is no interruption in benefits` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`s 2031(b)(7) selection is accomplished by assigning families that are determined eligible for or participating in the part A of title IV program or the supplemental nutrition assistance program` way) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the lead-in of paragraph (7)
        IF `there is an interruption in benefits for a family participating in the part A of title IV program or the supplemental nutrition assistance program` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "so that there is no interruption in benefits"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE   -- TRUE-kind: "no interruption in benefits"

-- (b)(8) "Paragraphs (1)(B) and (8) of section 2020(e) of this title shall apply with respect to applicants and participating
-- families in the same manner as such paragraphs apply with respect to applicants and participants in the supplemental nutrition
-- assistance program." This borrows what those paragraphs say, which is the answer of s 2020 (SEAMS.md).
-- src:2886 | (8) Paragraphs (1)(B) and (8) of section 2020(e) of this title shall apply with respect to applicants and participating families in the same manner as such paragraphs apply with respect to applicants and participants in the supplemental nutrition assistance program.
@ref s 2031(b)(8) paragraphs (1)(B) and (8) of section 2020(e) apply (src:2886)
GIVEN `the person is an applicant for the Project` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a participating family` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2031(b)(8) paragraphs (1)(B) and (8) of section 2020(e) apply to the person` MEANS
    IF `the person is an applicant for the Project` OR `the person is a participating family`
    THEN JUST TRUE   -- TRUE-kind: "shall apply with respect to applicants and participating families in the same manner"
    ELSE NOTHING     -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the paragraphs apply to "applicants and participating families"

-- (b)(9) "Assistance provided under the Project shall be reduced to reflect the pro rata value of any benefits received under the
-- supplemental nutrition assistance program for the same period." Fork FR-31-3: the reduced assistance is never below nothing.
-- src:2887 | (9) Assistance provided under the Project shall be reduced to reflect the pro rata value of any benefits received under the supplemental nutrition assistance program for the same period.
@ref s 2031(b)(9) reduction for benefits received (src:2887)
GIVEN `the assistance provided under the Project for the period, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the pro rata value of the benefits received under the supplemental nutrition assistance program for the same period, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 2031(b)(9) the assistance after the reduction, in dollars` MEANS
    IF `the assistance provided under the Project for the period, in dollars` GREATER THAN `the pro rata value of the benefits received under the supplemental nutrition assistance program for the same period, in dollars`
    THEN `the assistance provided under the Project for the period, in dollars` MINUS `the pro rata value of the benefits received under the supplemental nutrition assistance program for the same period, in dollars`   -- "reduced to reflect the pro rata value"
    ELSE 0   -- the reduction reaches the whole of the assistance, and the text does not say it can go below nothing (fork FR-31-3)

-- (b)(10)(A) "The State shall provide each family or family member whose participation in the Project ends and each family whose
-- participation is terminated with notice of the existence of the supplemental nutrition assistance program and the person or
-- agency to contact for more information."
