-- src:2896 | (13) The State shall carry out the supplemental nutrition assistance program throughout the State while the State carries out the Project.
@ref s 2031(b)(13) (the decision) (src:2896)
GIVEN `the State carries out the Project` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the State carries out the supplemental nutrition assistance program throughout the State` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2031(b)(13) the State has carried out the supplemental nutrition assistance program as the text requires` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the State carries out the Project` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty is "while the State carries out the Project"
        IF `the State carries out the supplemental nutrition assistance program throughout the State` THEN JUST TRUE   -- TRUE-kind: "shall carry out the supplemental nutrition assistance program throughout the State"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text says what the State shall do and not what follows if it does not

-- (b)(14)(A) "Except as provided in subparagraph (B), the State will carry out the Project during a five-year period beginning on
-- the date the first family receives assistance under the Project." Fork FR-31-4: the period ends on the day before the fifth
-- anniversary of the date the first family receives assistance. (On the stable binary `Date 29 2 2029` is `Date 1 3 2029`, so a
-- period begun on 29 February 2024 ends on 28 February 2029.)
-- src:2898 | (A) Except as provided in subparagraph (B), the State will carry out the Project during a five-year period beginning on the date the first family receives assistance under the Project.
@ref s 2031(b)(14)(A) the five-year period (src:2898)
GIVEN `the date the first family receives assistance under the Project` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 2031(b)(14)(A) the last day of the five-year period` MEANS
    Date (Day (Date (DATE_DAY `the date the first family receives assistance under the Project`) (DATE_MONTH `the date the first family receives assistance under the Project`) (DATE_YEAR `the date the first family receives assistance under the Project` PLUS 5)) MINUS 1)

-- src:2898 | (A) Except as provided in subparagraph (B), the State will carry out the Project during a five-year period beginning on the date the first family receives assistance under the Project.
@ref s 2031(b)(14)(A) the State carries out the Project in the period (src:2898)
GIVEN `the date the first family receives assistance under the Project` IS A DATE
      `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 2031(b)(14)(A) the day falls in the five-year period` MEANS
    `the day` AT LEAST `the date the first family receives assistance under the Project` AND `the day` AT MOST `s 2031(b)(14)(A) the last day of the five-year period` `the date the first family receives assistance under the Project`

-- (b)(14)(B) "The Project may be terminated (i) by the State one hundred and eighty days after the State gives notice to the
-- Secretary that it intends to terminate the Project; (ii) by the Secretary one hundred and eighty days after the Secretary, after
-- notice and an opportunity for a hearing, determines that the State materially failed to comply with this section; or (iii)
-- whenever the State and the Secretary jointly agree to terminate the Project." The function gives the first day on which the route
-- allows termination: the date of the notice, determination or agreement, plus 180 days for (i) and (ii).
-- src:2899 | (B) The Project may be terminated—
-- src:2900 | (i) by the State one hundred and eighty days after the State gives notice to the Secretary that it intends to terminate the Project;
-- src:2901 | (ii) by the Secretary one hundred and eighty days after the Secretary, after notice and an opportunity for a hearing, determines that the State materially failed to comply with this section; or
-- src:2902 | (iii) whenever the State and the Secretary jointly agree to terminate the Project.
@ref s 2031(b)(14)(B) termination of the Project (src:2899-2902)
GIVEN route IS A `s 2031 who terminates the Project`
      `the date of the State's notice, of the Secretary's determination, or of the agreement` IS A DATE
      `the Secretary gave notice and an opportunity for a hearing before determining that the State materially failed to comply with this section` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 2031(b)(14)(B) the first day on which the Project may be terminated` MEANS
    CONSIDER route
    WHEN `s 2031 the State, on notice to the Secretary` THEN JUST (Date (Day `the date of the State's notice, of the Secretary's determination, or of the agreement` PLUS 180))   -- TRUE-kind: "(i) by the State one hundred and eighty days after the State gives notice to the Secretary"
    WHEN `s 2031 the Secretary, after notice and an opportunity for a hearing, on finding that the State materially failed to comply` THEN
        IF `the Secretary gave notice and an opportunity for a hearing before determining that the State materially failed to comply with this section`
        THEN JUST (Date (Day `the date of the State's notice, of the Secretary's determination, or of the agreement` PLUS 180))   -- TRUE-kind: "(ii) by the Secretary one hundred and eighty days after the Secretary, after notice and an opportunity for a hearing, determines"
        ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "after notice and an opportunity for a hearing"
    WHEN `s 2031 the State and the Secretary jointly agree` THEN JUST `the date of the State's notice, of the Secretary's determination, or of the agreement`   -- TRUE-kind: "(iii) whenever the State and the Secretary jointly agree to terminate the Project"

-- (b)(15) "Not more than six thousand families may participate in the Project simultaneously."
-- src:2903 | (15) Not more than six thousand families may participate in the Project simultaneously.
@ref s 2031(b)(15) six thousand families (src:2903)
GIVEN `the number of families participating in the Project simultaneously` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2031(b)(15) the number of families participating simultaneously is within the limit` MEANS
    IF `the number of families participating in the Project simultaneously` AT MOST 6000
    THEN JUST TRUE   -- TRUE-kind: "Not more than six thousand families" is respected
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Not more than six thousand families may participate in the Project simultaneously"

§§ `(c) Additional terms and conditions of Project`

-- (c) "The Project shall be subject to the following additional terms and conditions".
-- (c)(1) "The State may require any parent in a participating family to participate in education, employment, or training
-- requirements unless the individual is a parent in a family with one parent who— (A) is ill, incapacitated, or sixty years of
-- age or older; (B) is needed in the home because of the illness or incapacity of another family member; (C) is the parent of a
-- child under one year of age and is personally providing care for the child; (D) is the parent of a child under six years of age
-- and is employed or participating in education or employment and training services for twenty or more hours a week; (E) works
-- thirty or more hours a week or, if the number of hours worked cannot be verified, earns at least the Federal minimum hourly wage
-- rate multiplied by thirty per week; or (F) is in the second or third trimester of pregnancy."
-- "May ... unless" withholds the permission from an exempt parent; this encoding counts that as the text's no (marginal reading
-- (a)). The Federal minimum hourly wage rate is not in this text, so it is an input, in dollars.
-- src:2906 | (1) The State may require any parent in a participating family to participate in education, employment, or training requirements unless the individual is a parent in a family with one parent who—
-- src:2907 | (A) is ill, incapacitated, or sixty years of age or older;
-- src:2908 | (B) is needed in the home because of the illness or incapacity of another family member;
-- src:2909 | (C) is the parent of a child under one year of age and is personally providing care for the child;
-- src:2910 | (D) is the parent of a child under six years of age and is employed or participating in education or employment and training services for twenty or more hours a week;
-- src:2911 | (E) works thirty or more hours a week or, if the number of hours worked cannot be verified, earns at least the Federal minimum hourly wage rate multiplied by thirty per week; or
-- src:2912 | (F) is in the second or third trimester of pregnancy.
@ref s 2031(c)(1) the State may require a parent to participate (src:2906-2912)
GIVEN parent IS A `s 2031 parent`
      `the Federal minimum hourly wage rate, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2031(c)(1) the State may require the parent to participate in education, employment, or training requirements` MEANS
    IF parent's `the family has one parent` AND (exemptA OR exemptB OR exemptC OR exemptD OR exemptE OR exemptF)
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The State may require any parent ... unless the individual is a parent in a family with one parent who" meets one of (A) to (F)
    ELSE JUST TRUE    -- TRUE-kind: "The State may require any parent in a participating family to participate in education, employment, or training requirements"
    WHERE
        exemptA MEANS parent's `the parent is ill or incapacitated` OR parent's `the parent's age in years` AT LEAST 60   -- (A) "is ill, incapacitated, or sixty years of age or older"
        exemptB MEANS parent's `the parent is needed in the home because of the illness or incapacity of another family member`   -- (B)
        exemptC MEANS parent's `the age of the parent's youngest child in months, or a negative number if the parent has no child` AT LEAST 0 AND parent's `the age of the parent's youngest child in months, or a negative number if the parent has no child` LESS THAN 12 AND parent's `the parent personally provides care for the child`   -- (C) "the parent of a child under one year of age and is personally providing care for the child"
        exemptD MEANS parent's `the age of the parent's youngest child in months, or a negative number if the parent has no child` AT LEAST 0 AND parent's `the age of the parent's youngest child in months, or a negative number if the parent has no child` LESS THAN 72 AND parent's `the hours a week the parent is employed or participates in education or employment and training services` AT LEAST 20   -- (D) "the parent of a child under six years of age and is employed or participating ... for twenty or more hours a week"
        exemptE MEANS IF parent's `the number of hours the parent works a week can be verified` THEN parent's `the hours a week the parent works, if they can be verified` AT LEAST 30 ELSE parent's `the parent's earnings a week` AT LEAST `the Federal minimum hourly wage rate, in dollars` TIMES 30   -- (E) "works thirty or more hours a week or, if the number of hours worked cannot be verified, earns at least the Federal minimum hourly wage rate multiplied by thirty per week"
        exemptF MEANS parent's `the trimester of pregnancy, or 0 if the parent is not pregnant` AT LEAST 2   -- (F) "is in the second or third trimester of pregnancy"

-- (c)(2) "The State shall not require any parent of a child under six years of age in a participating family with only one parent
-- to be employed or participate in education or employment and training services for more than twenty hours a week."
-- A bar and nothing else: up to twenty hours is not granted here (subsection (c)(1) grants).
-- src:2913 | (2) The State shall not require any parent of a child under six years of age in a participating family with only one parent to be employed or participate in education or employment and training services for more than twenty hours a week.
@ref s 2031(c)(2) the twenty-hour ceiling (src:2913)
GIVEN parent IS A `s 2031 parent`
      `the hours a week the State requires the parent to be employed or to participate in education or employment and training services` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2031(c)(2) the State may require the parent to be employed or participate for the hours` MEANS
    IF parent's `the family has one parent` AND parent's `the age of the parent's youngest child in months, or a negative number if the parent has no child` AT LEAST 0 AND parent's `the age of the parent's youngest child in months, or a negative number if the parent has no child` LESS THAN 72 AND `the hours a week the State requires the parent to be employed or to participate in education or employment and training services` GREATER THAN 20
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall not require any parent of a child under six years of age ... with only one parent to be employed or participate ... for more than twenty hours a week"
    ELSE NOTHING      -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "shall not require ... more than twenty hours" bars and grants nothing; up to twenty hours, and any other parent, are not covered

-- (c)(3) "For any period during which an individual required to participate in education, employment, or training requirements
-- fails to comply without good cause with a requirement imposed by the State under paragraph (1), the amount of assistance to the
-- family under the Project may be reduced by an amount not more than 10 percent of the assistance the family would be eligible
-- for with no income other than that from the Project."
-- src:2914 | (3) For any period during which an individual required to participate in education, employment, or training requirements fails to comply without good cause with a requirement imposed by the State under paragraph (1), the amount of assistance to the family under the Project may be reduced by an amount not more than 10 percent of the assistance the family would be eligible for with no income other than that from the Project.
@ref s 2031(c)(3) the most the assistance may be reduced by (src:2914)
GIVEN `the individual is required to participate in education, employment, or training requirements under paragraph (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the individual fails to comply with the requirement without good cause` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the assistance the family would be eligible for with no income other than that from the Project, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 2031(c)(3) the most the assistance to the family may be reduced by, in dollars` MEANS
    IF `the individual is required to participate in education, employment, or training requirements under paragraph (1)` AND `the individual fails to comply with the requirement without good cause`
    THEN JUST (10 DIVIDED BY 100 TIMES `the assistance the family would be eligible for with no income other than that from the Project, in dollars`)   -- "an amount not more than 10 percent of the assistance the family would be eligible for with no income other than that from the Project"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the reduction is for "any period during which an individual required ... fails to comply without good cause"

-- src:2914 | (3) For any period during which an individual required to participate in education, employment, or training requirements fails to comply without good cause with a requirement imposed by the State under paragraph (1), the amount of assistance to the family under the Project may be reduced by an amount not more than 10 percent of the assistance the family would be eligible for with no income other than that from the Project.
@ref s 2031(c)(3) a reduction within the limit (src:2914)
GIVEN `the individual is required to participate in education, employment, or training requirements under paragraph (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the individual fails to comply with the requirement without good cause` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the assistance the family would be eligible for with no income other than that from the Project, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the reduction, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2031(c)(3) the assistance to the family may be reduced by the amount` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the individual is required to participate in education, employment, or training requirements under paragraph (1)` AND `the individual fails to comply with the requirement without good cause`) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the reduction is for "any period during which an individual required ... fails to comply without good cause"
        IF `the reduction, in dollars` AT MOST 10 DIVIDED BY 100 TIMES `the assistance the family would be eligible for with no income other than that from the Project, in dollars` THEN JUST TRUE   -- TRUE-kind: "may be reduced by an amount not more than 10 percent"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "an amount not more than 10 percent of the assistance the family would be eligible for"

§§ `(d) Funding`

-- (d)(1)(A) "If an application submitted under subsection (a) complies with the requirements specified in subsection (b), then the
