-- src:2919 | (i) the cost of food assistance provided under the Project equal to the amount that would have otherwise been issued in the form of benefits under the supplemental nutrition assistance program had the Project not been implemented, as estimated under a methodology satisfactory to the Secretary after negotiations with the State; and
@ref s 2031(d)(1)(B) the Secretary's duty to pay the State each calendar quarter (src:2918-2919)
`s 2031(d)(1)(B) the Secretary's duty to pay the State each calendar quarter` MEANS
    PARTY `the Secretary`
    MUST `s 2031 pay the State each calendar quarter`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the Secretary` BECAUSE "the Secretary did not pay the State for a calendar quarter"

-- src:2918 | (B) subject to subsection (b)(12) from the funds appropriated under this chapter provide grant awards and pay the State each calendar quarter for—
-- src:2919 | (i) the cost of food assistance provided under the Project equal to the amount that would have otherwise been issued in the form of benefits under the supplemental nutrition assistance program had the Project not been implemented, as estimated under a methodology satisfactory to the Secretary after negotiations with the State; and
@ref s 2031(d)(1)(B)(i) the payment for the cost of food assistance (src:2918-2919)
GIVEN `the amount that would have been issued in the form of benefits under the supplemental nutrition assistance program had the Project not been implemented, as estimated under a methodology satisfactory to the Secretary, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the part of the limit in subsection (b)(12) not yet used in the fiscal year, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 2031(d)(1)(B)(i) the payment for the cost of food assistance, in dollars` MEANS
    IF `the amount that would have been issued in the form of benefits under the supplemental nutrition assistance program had the Project not been implemented, as estimated under a methodology satisfactory to the Secretary, in dollars` AT MOST `the part of the limit in subsection (b)(12) not yet used in the fiscal year, in dollars`
    THEN `the amount that would have been issued in the form of benefits under the supplemental nutrition assistance program had the Project not been implemented, as estimated under a methodology satisfactory to the Secretary, in dollars`   -- "equal to the amount that would have otherwise been issued in the form of benefits"
    ELSE `the part of the limit in subsection (b)(12) not yet used in the fiscal year, in dollars`   -- "subject to subsection (b)(12)"

-- (d)(1)(B)(ii) "the administrative costs incurred by the State to provide food assistance under the Project that are authorized
-- under subsections (a), (g), (h)(2), and (h)(3) of section 2025 of this title equal to the amount that otherwise would have been
-- paid under such subsections had the Project not been implemented, as estimated under a methodology satisfactory to the
-- Secretary after negotiations with the State: Provided, That payments made under subsection (g) of section 2025 of this title
-- shall equal payments that would have been made if the Project had not been implemented." The amounts under s 2025 are its answers.
-- src:2920 | (ii) the administrative costs incurred by the State to provide food assistance under the Project that are authorized under subsections (a), (g), (h)(2), and (h)(3) of section 2025 of this title equal to the amount that otherwise would have been paid under such subsections had the Project not been implemented, as estimated under a methodology satisfactory to the Secretary after negotiations with the State: Provided, That payments made under subsection (g) of section 2025 of this title shall equal payments that would have been made if the Project had not been implemented.
@ref s 2031(d)(1)(B)(ii) the payment for administrative costs (src:2920)
GIVEN `s 2025 the amount that otherwise would have been paid under subsections (a), (g), (h)(2) and (h)(3) of section 2025 had the Project not been implemented, as estimated under a methodology satisfactory to the Secretary, in dollars` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `the administrative costs incurred by the State to provide food assistance under the Project that are authorized under those subsections, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 2031(d)(1)(B)(ii) the payment for administrative costs, in dollars` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 2025 the amount that otherwise would have been paid under subsections (a), (g), (h)(2) and (h)(3) of section 2025 had the Project not been implemented, as estimated under a methodology satisfactory to the Secretary, in dollars`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the amount section 2025 would have paid was not supplied
    WHEN JUST wouldHave THEN
        JUST (IF `the administrative costs incurred by the State to provide food assistance under the Project that are authorized under those subsections, in dollars` AT MOST wouldHave THEN `the administrative costs incurred by the State to provide food assistance under the Project that are authorized under those subsections, in dollars` ELSE wouldHave)   -- fork FR-31-8: the payment is the amount section 2025 would have paid, and never more than the costs incurred ("the administrative costs incurred by the State ... equal to the amount that otherwise would have been paid")

-- src:2920 | (ii) the administrative costs incurred by the State to provide food assistance under the Project that are authorized under subsections (a), (g), (h)(2), and (h)(3) of section 2025 of this title equal to the amount that otherwise would have been paid under such subsections had the Project not been implemented, as estimated under a methodology satisfactory to the Secretary after negotiations with the State: Provided, That payments made under subsection (g) of section 2025 of this title shall equal payments that would have been made if the Project had not been implemented.
@ref s 2031(d)(1)(B)(ii) the proviso on payments under section 2025(g) (src:2920)
GIVEN `the payments made under subsection (g) of section 2025, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the payments that would have been made if the Project had not been implemented, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2031(d)(1)(B)(ii) the payments under subsection (g) of section 2025 are as the proviso requires` MEANS
    IF `the payments made under subsection (g) of section 2025, in dollars` EQUALS `the payments that would have been made if the Project had not been implemented, in dollars`
    THEN JUST TRUE   -- TRUE-kind: "shall equal payments that would have been made if the Project had not been implemented"
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall equal payments that would have been made"

-- (d)(2) "The Secretary shall periodically adjust payments made to the State under paragraph (1) to reflect— (A) the cost of
-- benefits issued to individuals ineligible for the Project specified in subsection (b)(3)(E) in excess of the amount that would
-- have been issued to such individuals had the Project not been implemented, as estimated under a methodology satisfactory to the
-- Secretary after negotiations with the State; and (B) the cost of benefits issued to families exercising the option specified in
-- subsection (b)(3)(D)(iii) in excess of the amount that would have been issued to such individuals had the Project not been implemented".
-- src:2921 | (2) The Secretary shall periodically adjust payments made to the State under paragraph (1) to reflect—
@ref s 2031(d)(2) the Secretary's duty to adjust payments (src:2921)
`s 2031(d)(2) the Secretary's duty to adjust the payments made to the State` MEANS
    PARTY `the Secretary`
    MUST `s 2031 adjust the payments made to the State`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the Secretary` BECAUSE "the Secretary did not periodically adjust the payments made to the State"

-- src:2922 | (A) the cost of benefits issued to individuals ineligible for the Project specified in subsection (b)(3)(E) in excess of the amount that would have been issued to such individuals had the Project not been implemented, as estimated under a methodology satisfactory to the Secretary after negotiations with the State; and
@ref s 2031(d)(2)(A) the adjustment for individuals ineligible for the Project (src:2922)
GIVEN `the cost of benefits issued to individuals ineligible for the Project specified in subsection (b)(3)(E), in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount that would have been issued to such individuals had the Project not been implemented, as estimated under a methodology satisfactory to the Secretary, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 2031(d)(2)(A) the adjustment for benefits issued to individuals ineligible for the Project, in dollars` MEANS
    IF `the cost of benefits issued to individuals ineligible for the Project specified in subsection (b)(3)(E), in dollars` GREATER THAN `the amount that would have been issued to such individuals had the Project not been implemented, as estimated under a methodology satisfactory to the Secretary, in dollars`
    THEN `the cost of benefits issued to individuals ineligible for the Project specified in subsection (b)(3)(E), in dollars` MINUS `the amount that would have been issued to such individuals had the Project not been implemented, as estimated under a methodology satisfactory to the Secretary, in dollars`   -- "the cost of benefits issued ... in excess of the amount that would have been issued"
    ELSE 0   -- no excess, no adjustment (fork FR-31-9: an adjustment under (d)(2) is only for the excess and is never negative)

-- src:2923 | (B) the cost of benefits issued to families exercising the option specified in subsection (b)(3)(D)(iii) in excess of the amount that would have been issued to such individuals had the Project not been implemented, as estimated under a methodology satisfactory to the Secretary after negotiations with the State.
@ref s 2031(d)(2)(B) the adjustment for families exercising the option (src:2923)
GIVEN `the cost of benefits issued to families exercising the option specified in subsection (b)(3)(D)(iii), in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount that would have been issued had the Project not been implemented, as estimated under a methodology satisfactory to the Secretary, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 2031(d)(2)(B) the adjustment for benefits issued to families exercising the option, in dollars` MEANS
    IF `the cost of benefits issued to families exercising the option specified in subsection (b)(3)(D)(iii), in dollars` GREATER THAN `the amount that would have been issued had the Project not been implemented, as estimated under a methodology satisfactory to the Secretary, in dollars`
    THEN `the cost of benefits issued to families exercising the option specified in subsection (b)(3)(D)(iii), in dollars` MINUS `the amount that would have been issued had the Project not been implemented, as estimated under a methodology satisfactory to the Secretary, in dollars`   -- "the cost of benefits issued ... in excess of the amount that would have been issued"
    ELSE 0   -- no excess, no adjustment (fork FR-31-9)

-- (d)(3) "Payments under paragraph (1)(B) shall include adjustments, as estimated under a methodology satisfactory to the
-- Secretary after negotiations with the State, for increases or decreases in the costs of providing food assistance and associated
-- administrative costs that result from changes in economic, demographic, or other conditions in the State based on data specific
-- to the State, changes in eligibility or benefit levels authorized by this chapter, and changes in or additional amounts of
-- Federal funds available to States and localities under the supplemental nutrition assistance program."
-- src:2924 | (3) Payments under paragraph (1)(B) shall include adjustments, as estimated under a methodology satisfactory to the Secretary after negotiations with the State, for increases or decreases in the costs of providing food assistance and associated administrative costs that result from changes in economic, demographic, or other conditions in the State based on data specific to the State, changes in eligibility or benefit levels authorized by this chapter, and changes in or additional amounts of Federal funds available to States and localities under the supplemental nutrition assistance program.
@ref s 2031(d)(3) the payment including the adjustments (src:2924)
GIVEN `the payment under paragraph (1)(B) before the adjustments, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the increases (positive) or decreases (negative) in the costs of providing food assistance and associated administrative costs that result from the changes the paragraph names, as estimated under a methodology satisfactory to the Secretary, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 2031(d)(3) the payment under paragraph (1)(B) including the adjustments, in dollars` MEANS
    `the payment under paragraph (1)(B) before the adjustments, in dollars` PLUS `the increases (positive) or decreases (negative) in the costs of providing food assistance and associated administrative costs that result from the changes the paragraph names, as estimated under a methodology satisfactory to the Secretary, in dollars`   -- "shall include adjustments ... for increases or decreases in the costs"

§§ `(e) Waiver`

-- (e) "With respect to the Project, the Secretary shall waive compliance with any requirement contained in this chapter (other than
-- this section) that, if applied, would prevent the State from carrying out the Project or effectively achieving its purpose."
-- src:2926 | With respect to the Project, the Secretary shall waive compliance with any requirement contained in this chapter (other than this section) that, if applied, would prevent the State from carrying out the Project or effectively achieving its purpose.
@ref s 2031(e) the Secretary's duty to waive compliance (src:2926)
`s 2031(e) the Secretary's duty to waive compliance` MEANS
    PARTY `the Secretary`
    MUST `s 2031 waive compliance with a requirement of this chapter`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the Secretary` BECAUSE "the Secretary did not waive compliance with a requirement of this chapter that would prevent the State from carrying out the Project or effectively achieving its purpose"

-- src:2926 | With respect to the Project, the Secretary shall waive compliance with any requirement contained in this chapter (other than this section) that, if applied, would prevent the State from carrying out the Project or effectively achieving its purpose.
@ref s 2031(e) (the decision) (src:2926)
GIVEN `the requirement is contained in this section` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the requirement, if applied, would prevent the State from carrying out the Project or effectively achieving its purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2031(e) the Secretary shall waive compliance with the requirement` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the requirement is contained in this section` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any requirement contained in this chapter (other than this section)" (the text does not say a requirement of this section may not be waived, it only does not require the waiver)
        IF `the requirement, if applied, would prevent the State from carrying out the Project or effectively achieving its purpose` THEN JUST TRUE   -- TRUE-kind: "shall waive compliance with any requirement ... that, if applied, would prevent the State from carrying out the Project or effectively achieving its purpose"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty is for a requirement that "would prevent the State"; a waiver of any other is neither required nor barred

§§ `(f) Project audits`

-- (f) "The Comptroller General of the United States shall— (1) conduct periodic audits of the operation of the Project to verify
-- the amounts payable to the State from time to time under subsection (d); and (2) submit to the Secretary, the Secretary of
-- Health and Human Services, the Committee on Agriculture of the House of Representatives, and the Committee on Agriculture,
-- Nutrition, and Forestry of the Senate a report describing the results of each such audit." The core has no party for the
-- Comptroller General (NEEDS-CORE.md), so these are decisions over facts and not regulative rules.
-- src:2928 | The Comptroller General of the United States shall—
-- src:2929 | (1) conduct periodic audits of the operation of the Project to verify the amounts payable to the State from time to time under subsection (d); and
@ref s 2031(f)(1) periodic audits (src:2928-2929)
GIVEN `the Comptroller General has conducted periodic audits of the operation of the Project to verify the amounts payable to the State from time to time under subsection (d)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2031(f)(1) the Comptroller General has conducted the audits the text requires` MEANS
    IF `the Comptroller General has conducted periodic audits of the operation of the Project to verify the amounts payable to the State from time to time under subsection (d)`
    THEN JUST TRUE   -- TRUE-kind: "shall conduct periodic audits of the operation of the Project"
    ELSE NOTHING     -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "periodic" is not defined and the text says nothing of what follows if no audit is made

-- src:2930 | (2) submit to the Secretary, the Secretary of Health and Human Services, the Committee on Agriculture of the House of Representatives, and the Committee on Agriculture, Nutrition, and Forestry of the Senate a report describing the results of each such audit.
@ref s 2031(f)(2) the report of each audit (src:2930)
GIVEN `the report describing the results of the audit has been submitted to the Secretary` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it has been submitted to the Secretary of Health and Human Services` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it has been submitted to the Committee on Agriculture of the House of Representatives` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it has been submitted to the Committee on Agriculture, Nutrition, and Forestry of the Senate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2031(f)(2) the Comptroller General has submitted the report of the audit to all four recipients` MEANS
    IF `the report describing the results of the audit has been submitted to the Secretary` AND `it has been submitted to the Secretary of Health and Human Services` AND `it has been submitted to the Committee on Agriculture of the House of Representatives` AND `it has been submitted to the Committee on Agriculture, Nutrition, and Forestry of the Senate`
    THEN JUST TRUE   -- TRUE-kind: "submit to the Secretary, the Secretary of Health and Human Services, the Committee on Agriculture ..., and the Committee on Agriculture, Nutrition, and Forestry ... a report describing the results of each such audit"
    ELSE NOTHING     -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text sets no time for the report and says nothing of what follows if a recipient is missed

§§ `(g) Construction`

-- (g)(1) "For purposes of any Federal, State, or local law other than part A of title IV of the Social Security Act or this chapter—
-- (A) cash assistance provided under the Project that is designated as food assistance by the State shall be treated in the same
-- manner as benefits allotments under the supplemental nutrition assistance program are treated".
-- src:2932 | (1) For purposes of any Federal, State, or local law other than part A of title IV of the Social Security Act [42 U.S.C. 601 et seq.] or this chapter—
-- src:2933 | (A) cash assistance provided under the Project that is designated as food assistance by the State shall be treated in the same manner as benefits allotments under the supplemental nutrition assistance program are treated; and
@ref s 2031(g)(1)(A) cash assistance designated as food assistance (src:2932-2933)
GIVEN `the law is part A of title IV of the Social Security Act or this chapter` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the cash assistance is provided under the Project and designated as food assistance by the State` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2031(g)(1)(A) the cash assistance is treated in the same manner as benefit allotments under the supplemental nutrition assistance program` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the law is part A of title IV of the Social Security Act or this chapter` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "For purposes of any Federal, State, or local law other than part A of title IV ... or this chapter"
        IF `the cash assistance is provided under the Project and designated as food assistance by the State` THEN JUST TRUE   -- TRUE-kind: "cash assistance provided under the Project that is designated as food assistance by the State shall be treated in the same manner as benefits allotments"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): only cash assistance "designated as food assistance by the State"

-- (g)(1)(B) "participating families shall be treated in the same manner as participants in the supplemental nutrition assistance program are treated."
-- src:2934 | (B) participating families shall be treated in the same manner as participants in the supplemental nutrition assistance program are treated.
@ref s 2031(g)(1)(B) participating families (src:2934)
GIVEN `the law is part A of title IV of the Social Security Act or this chapter` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the family participates in the Project` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2031(g)(1)(B) the family is treated in the same manner as a participant in the supplemental nutrition assistance program` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the law is part A of title IV of the Social Security Act or this chapter` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "For purposes of any Federal, State, or local law other than part A of title IV ... or this chapter"
        IF `the family participates in the Project` THEN JUST TRUE   -- TRUE-kind: "participating families shall be treated in the same manner as participants in the supplemental nutrition assistance program are treated"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "participating families"

-- (g)(2)(A) "Nothing in this section shall— (A) allow payments made to the State under the Project to be less than the amounts the
-- State and eligible households within the State would have received if the Project had not been implemented".
-- src:2935 | (2) Nothing in this section shall—
-- src:2936 | (A) allow payments made to the State under the Project to be less than the amounts the State and eligible households within the State would have received if the Project had not been implemented; or
@ref s 2031(g)(2)(A) payments are not less than they would have been (src:2935-2936)
GIVEN `the payments made to the State under the Project, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the amounts the State and eligible households within the State would have received if the Project had not been implemented, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2031(g)(2)(A) this section allows the payments made to the State` MEANS
    IF `the payments made to the State under the Project, in dollars` AT LEAST `the amounts the State and eligible households within the State would have received if the Project had not been implemented, in dollars`
    THEN NOTHING     -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Nothing in this section shall allow payments ... to be less" bars and grants nothing; payments at or above the amounts are not touched by it
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Nothing in this section shall allow payments made to the State under the Project to be less than the amounts the State and eligible households ... would have received"

-- (g)(2)(B) "Nothing in this section shall ... (B) require the Secretary to incur costs as a result of the Project in excess of
-- costs that would have been incurred if the Project had not been implemented, except for costs for evaluation."
-- src:2937 | (B) require the Secretary to incur costs as a result of the Project in excess of costs that would have been incurred if the Project had not been implemented, except for costs for evaluation.
@ref s 2031(g)(2)(B) no costs in excess (src:2937)
GIVEN `the costs the Secretary incurs as a result of the Project, other than costs for evaluation, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the costs that would have been incurred if the Project had not been implemented, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2031(g)(2)(B) this section requires the Secretary to incur the costs` MEANS
    IF `the costs the Secretary incurs as a result of the Project, other than costs for evaluation, in dollars` GREATER THAN `the costs that would have been incurred if the Project had not been implemented, in dollars`
    THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Nothing in this section shall require the Secretary to incur costs ... in excess of costs that would have been incurred"
    ELSE NOTHING     -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Nothing in this section shall require" bars and grants nothing; costs for evaluation are outside it (subsection (i)(2))

§§ `(h) Quality control`

-- (h) "Participating families shall be excluded from any sample taken for purposes of making any determination under section
-- 2025(c) of this title."
-- src:2939 | Participating families shall be excluded from any sample taken for purposes of making any determination under section 2025(c) of this title. For purposes of establishing the total value of allotments under section 2025(c)(1) of this title, benefits and the amount of federal liability for food assistance provided under the Project as limited by subsection (b)(12) of this section shall be treated as allotments issued under the supplemental nutrition assistance program.
@ref s 2031(h) excluded from the sample (src:2939)
GIVEN `the family participates in the Project` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2031(h) the family is excluded from the sample` MEANS
    IF `the family participates in the Project`
    THEN JUST TRUE   -- TRUE-kind: "Participating families shall be excluded from any sample taken for purposes of making any determination under section 2025(c)"
    ELSE NOTHING     -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the exclusion is of "participating families"

-- (h) "For purposes of establishing the total value of allotments under section 2025(c)(1) of this title, benefits and the amount
-- of federal liability for food assistance provided under the Project as limited by subsection (b)(12) of this section shall be
-- treated as allotments issued under the supplemental nutrition assistance program." Fork FR-31-10: the total counted is the
-- allotments, plus the benefits, plus the federal liability for food assistance, which is never counted above the (b)(12) limit.
-- src:2939 | Participating families shall be excluded from any sample taken for purposes of making any determination under section 2025(c) of this title. For purposes of establishing the total value of allotments under section 2025(c)(1) of this title, benefits and the amount of federal liability for food assistance provided under the Project as limited by subsection (b)(12) of this section shall be treated as allotments issued under the supplemental nutrition assistance program.
@ref s 2031(h) the total value of allotments (src:2939)
GIVEN `the value of the allotments issued under the supplemental nutrition assistance program, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the benefits issued under the Project, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the federal liability for food assistance provided under the Project, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the limit of subsection (b)(12), in dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 2031(h) the total value of allotments under section 2025(c)(1), in dollars` MEANS
    `the value of the allotments issued under the supplemental nutrition assistance program, in dollars` PLUS `the benefits issued under the Project, in dollars` PLUS (IF `the federal liability for food assistance provided under the Project, in dollars` AT MOST `the limit of subsection (b)(12), in dollars` THEN `the federal liability for food assistance provided under the Project, in dollars` ELSE `the limit of subsection (b)(12), in dollars`)   -- "benefits and the amount of federal liability for food assistance provided under the Project as limited by subsection (b)(12) ... shall be treated as allotments issued"

§§ `(i) Evaluation`

-- (i)(1) the concerns "such as effects on benefits to participants, costs of the Project, payment accuracy, administrative
-- consequences, any reduction in welfare dependency, any reduction in total assistance payments, and the consequences of cash
-- payments on household expenditures, and food consumption". "Such as" does not close the list.
DECLARE `s 2031 evaluation concern` IS ONE OF
    `s 2031 effects on benefits to participants`
    `s 2031 costs of the Project`
    `s 2031 payment accuracy`
    `s 2031 administrative consequences`
    `s 2031 any reduction in welfare dependency`
    `s 2031 any reduction in total assistance payments`
    `s 2031 the consequences of cash payments on household expenditures`
    `s 2031 the consequences of cash payments on food consumption`
    `s 2031 some other concern`

-- (i)(1) "The State shall develop and implement a plan for an independent evaluation designed to provide reliable information on
-- Project impacts and implementation."
-- src:2941 | (1) The State shall develop and implement a plan for an independent evaluation designed to provide reliable information on Project impacts and implementation. The evaluation will include treatment and control groups and will include random assignment of families to treatment and control groups in an urban setting. The evaluation plan shall satisfy the evaluation concerns of the Secretary of Agriculture such as effects on benefits to participants, costs of the Project, payment accuracy, administrative consequences, any reduction in welfare dependency, any reduction in total assistance payments, and the consequences of cash payments on household expenditures, and food consumption. The evaluation plan shall take into consideration the evaluation requirements and administrative obligations of the State. The evaluation will measure the effects of the Project in regard to goals of increasing family income, prevention of long-term dependency, movement toward self-support, and simplification of the welfare system.
@ref s 2031(i)(1) the State agency's duty to develop and implement an evaluation plan (src:2941)
`s 2031(i)(1) the State agency's duty to develop and implement an evaluation plan` MEANS
    PARTY `the State agency`
    MUST `s 2031 develop and implement a plan for an independent evaluation`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the State agency` BECAUSE "the State agency did not develop and implement a plan for an independent evaluation"

-- src:2941 | (1) The State shall develop and implement a plan for an independent evaluation designed to provide reliable information on Project impacts and implementation. The evaluation will include treatment and control groups and will include random assignment of families to treatment and control groups in an urban setting. The evaluation plan shall satisfy the evaluation concerns of the Secretary of Agriculture such as effects on benefits to participants, costs of the Project, payment accuracy, administrative consequences, any reduction in welfare dependency, any reduction in total assistance payments, and the consequences of cash payments on household expenditures, and food consumption. The evaluation plan shall take into consideration the evaluation requirements and administrative obligations of the State. The evaluation will measure the effects of the Project in regard to goals of increasing family income, prevention of long-term dependency, movement toward self-support, and simplification of the welfare system.
@ref s 2031(i)(1) what the plan contains (src:2941)
GIVEN plan IS A `s 2031 evaluation plan`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2031(i)(1) the plan contains what the text requires` MEANS
    IF plan's `it provides for an independent evaluation designed to provide reliable information on Project impacts and implementation`
       AND plan's `it includes treatment and control groups with random assignment of families in an urban setting`
       AND plan's `it satisfies the evaluation concerns of the Secretary of Agriculture`
       AND plan's `it takes into consideration the evaluation requirements and administrative obligations of the State`
       AND plan's `it measures the effects of the Project on the goals of increasing family income, prevention of long-term dependency, movement toward self-support, and simplification of the welfare system`
    THEN JUST TRUE   -- TRUE-kind: "The State shall develop and implement a plan for an independent evaluation ... The evaluation will include treatment and control groups ... The evaluation plan shall satisfy the evaluation concerns ... shall take into consideration ... will measure the effects"
    ELSE NOTHING     -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text says what the plan shall contain and not what follows if it does not

-- src:2941 | (1) The State shall develop and implement a plan for an independent evaluation designed to provide reliable information on Project impacts and implementation. The evaluation will include treatment and control groups and will include random assignment of families to treatment and control groups in an urban setting. The evaluation plan shall satisfy the evaluation concerns of the Secretary of Agriculture such as effects on benefits to participants, costs of the Project, payment accuracy, administrative consequences, any reduction in welfare dependency, any reduction in total assistance payments, and the consequences of cash payments on household expenditures, and food consumption. The evaluation plan shall take into consideration the evaluation requirements and administrative obligations of the State. The evaluation will measure the effects of the Project in regard to goals of increasing family income, prevention of long-term dependency, movement toward self-support, and simplification of the welfare system.
@ref s 2031(i)(1) the evaluation concerns of the Secretary of Agriculture (src:2941)
GIVEN concern IS A `s 2031 evaluation concern`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2031(i)(1) the concern is one the evaluation plan shall satisfy` MEANS
    CONSIDER concern
    WHEN `s 2031 some other concern` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "such as" does not say these are the only concerns
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE   -- TRUE-kind: "such as effects on benefits to participants, costs of the Project, payment accuracy, administrative consequences, any reduction in welfare dependency, any reduction in total assistance payments, and the consequences of cash payments on household expenditures, and food consumption"

-- (i)(2) "The State shall pay 50 percent of the cost of developing and implementing such plan and the Federal Government shall pay the remainder."
-- src:2942 | (2) The State shall pay 50 percent of the cost of developing and implementing such plan and the Federal Government shall pay the remainder.
@ref s 2031(i)(2) the State's share (src:2942)
GIVEN `the cost of developing and implementing the plan, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 2031(i)(2) the State's share of the cost of the plan, in dollars` MEANS
    50 DIVIDED BY 100 TIMES `the cost of developing and implementing the plan, in dollars`   -- "The State shall pay 50 percent of the cost"

-- src:2942 | (2) The State shall pay 50 percent of the cost of developing and implementing such plan and the Federal Government shall pay the remainder.
@ref s 2031(i)(2) the Federal Government's share (src:2942)
GIVEN `the cost of developing and implementing the plan, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 2031(i)(2) the Federal Government's share of the cost of the plan, in dollars` MEANS
    `the cost of developing and implementing the plan, in dollars` MINUS `s 2031(i)(2) the State's share of the cost of the plan, in dollars` `the cost of developing and implementing the plan, in dollars`   -- "the Federal Government shall pay the remainder"

§§ `(j) Definitions`

-- (j)(1) "The term 'family' means the following individuals who live together: a minor child or a group of minor children related
-- to each other as siblings, half siblings, stepsiblings, or adopted siblings, together with their natural or adoptive parents, or
-- their caregiver. Family also includes a pregnant woman in the third trimester of pregnancy with no children."
-- "Means" is a definition, which this encoding counts as the text's no for a group it does not cover. The one case it leaves at
-- NOTHING is minor children related as siblings who live together with neither a parent nor a caregiver: the text names them
-- "together with" parents or a caregiver and does not say whether the parents or caregiver are required (fork FR-31-6).
-- src:2945 | (1) The term “family” means the following individuals who live together: a minor child or a group of minor children related to each other as siblings, half siblings, stepsiblings, or adopted siblings, together with their natural or adoptive parents, or their caregiver. Family also includes a pregnant woman in the third trimester of pregnancy with no children.
@ref s 2031(j)(1) family (src:2945)
GIVEN group IS A `s 2031 group`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2031(j)(1) the group is a family` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF group's `it is a pregnant woman in the third trimester of pregnancy with no children` THEN JUST TRUE   -- TRUE-kind: "Family also includes a pregnant woman in the third trimester of pregnancy with no children"
        IF group's `the number of minor children` LESS THAN 1 THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means a minor child or a group of minor children ... together with"; a definition is the text's no for a group it does not cover
        IF NOT group's `they live together` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the following individuals who live together"
        IF group's `the number of minor children` GREATER THAN 1 AND NOT group's `the minor children are related to each other as siblings, half siblings, stepsiblings, or adopted siblings` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a group of minor children related to each other as siblings, half siblings, stepsiblings, or adopted siblings"
        IF group's `a natural or adoptive parent of the children lives with them` OR group's `the children's caregiver lives with them` THEN JUST TRUE   -- TRUE-kind: "a minor child or a group of minor children ..., together with their natural or adoptive parents, or their caregiver"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): children living together with neither a parent nor a caregiver (fork FR-31-6)

-- (j)(2) "The term 'contract' means a plan to help a family pursue self-sufficiency, based on the State's assessment of the
-- family's needs and abilities and developed with a parental caregiver." "Parental caregiver" is not defined in this text
-- ((j)(3) defines "caregiver" and not "parental"), so whether the person is one is a conditional input.
-- src:2946 | (2) The term “contract” means a plan to help a family pursue self-sufficiency, based on the State’s assessment of the family’s needs and abilities and developed with a parental caregiver.
@ref s 2031(j)(2) contract (src:2946)
GIVEN `the document is a plan to help a family pursue self-sufficiency` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is based on the State's assessment of the family's needs and abilities` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person it was developed with is a parental caregiver` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2031(j)(2) the document is a contract` MEANS
    `s 2031 every one of these holds`
        (LIST JUST `the document is a plan to help a family pursue self-sufficiency`,
              JUST `it is based on the State's assessment of the family's needs and abilities`,
              `the person it was developed with is a parental caregiver`)   -- every limb of the definition; a missing limb is the text's no (a definition), an unsupplied "parental caregiver" is NOTHING (undefined term)

-- (j)(3) "The term 'caregiver' means a minor child's natural or adoptive parent or parents who live in the home with the minor
-- child. For purposes of determining eligibility for the Project, 'caregiver' also means any of the following individuals who
-- live with and provide care and support to a minor child when the minor child's natural or adoptive parent or parents do not
-- reside in the same home: grandfather, grandmother, brother, sister, stepfather, stepmother, stepbrother, stepsister, uncle, aunt,
-- first cousin, nephew, niece, persons of preceding generations as denoted by prefixes of 'great' or 'great-great' or a spouse of
-- any person named in the above groups even after the marriage ends by death or divorce."
-- src:2947 | (3) The term “caregiver” means a minor child’s natural or adoptive parent or parents who live in the home with the minor child. For purposes of determining eligibility for the Project, “caregiver” also means any of the following individuals who live with and provide care and support to a minor child when the minor child’s natural or adoptive parent or parents do not reside in the same home: grandfather, grandmother, brother, sister, stepfather, stepmother, stepbrother, stepsister, uncle, aunt, first cousin, nephew, niece, persons of preceding generations as denoted by prefixes of “great” or “great-great” or a spouse of any person named in the above groups even after the marriage ends by death or divorce.
@ref s 2031(j)(3) caregiver (src:2947)
GIVEN relationship IS A `s 2031 relationship to the minor child`
      `the person lives in the home with the minor child` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person provides care and support to the minor child` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a natural or adoptive parent of the minor child resides in the same home` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the purpose is determining eligibility for the Project` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2031(j)(3) the person is a caregiver` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF relationship EQUALS `s 2031 natural or adoptive parent` AND `the person lives in the home with the minor child` THEN JUST TRUE   -- TRUE-kind: "a minor child's natural or adoptive parent or parents who live in the home with the minor child"
        IF relationship EQUALS `s 2031 natural or adoptive parent` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): a parent who does not live in the home with the minor child is outside the first sentence; a definition is the text's no
        IF relationship EQUALS `s 2031 some other relationship` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): not a parent and not on the second sentence's list; a definition is the text's no
        IF NOT `the purpose is determining eligibility for the Project` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the second sentence is "For purposes of determining eligibility for the Project"
        IF `the person lives in the home with the minor child` AND `the person provides care and support to the minor child` AND NOT `a natural or adoptive parent of the minor child resides in the same home` THEN JUST TRUE   -- TRUE-kind: "any of the following individuals who live with and provide care and support to a minor child when the minor child's natural or adoptive parent or parents do not reside in the same home"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): a listed relative who does not live with and care for the child, or whose parent resides in the same home

-- (j)(4) "The term 'State' means the State of Minnesota."
-- src:2948 | (4) The term “State” means the State of Minnesota.
@ref s 2031(j)(4) State (src:2948)
GIVEN name IS A STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2031(j)(4) the name is the State` MEANS
    IF name EQUALS "Minnesota"
    THEN JUST TRUE   -- TRUE-kind: "The term 'State' means the State of Minnesota"
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): a definition is the text's no for any other place
